today I'm going to show you how to set  up an HTTP or HTTPS load balancer first  navigate to networking now navigate to  load balancing now click start  configuration in the HTTP HTTPS load  balancing section fill in the name of  your load balancer you can use lowercase  letters numbers and hyphens click  back-end configuration to configure  where your incoming traffic will be  redirected from the drop down menu you  can select an existing back-end service  or you can create a new back-end service  now enter the name for your back-end  service from the back-end section select  an instance group finally select a  health check from the drop down at the  bottom click host and path rules from  the left panel the first row determines  where any traffic not explicitly with a  host and path rule will be sent click  add host and path rule to add a second  row now fill it in click front-end  configuration to configure the protocol  IP address port and certificate if  necessary finally click the create  button to create your load balancer
 

